    "result_text": "The full build passes. \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the structured audit event for owner creation in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **Sequence counter** \u2014 added a process-wide `static final AtomicLong AUDIT_EVENT_SEQ`, so `seq` increases monotonically across every create regardless of controller instance.\n\n2. **Immutable event** \u2014 added a private `record OwnerCreatedEvent(long seq, Integer ownerId, String customerCode, Integer membershipLevel, String event)`, serialized to JSON with a Jackson `ObjectMapper`.\n\n3. **Emission** \u2014 `createdOwnerResponse` now also calls `emitOwnerCreatedEvent(...)`, which logs `{\"seq\":..,\"ownerId\":..,\"customerCode\":..,\"membershipLevel\":..,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}` on the `AUDIT` logger, right alongside the existing human-readable audit line.\n\n4. **Future-proof primary identifier** \u2014 the event's `customerCode` value comes from a small `primaryIdentifier(Owner)` helper that returns `owner.getCustomerCode()` today. When the customerCode is later unified into the memberId, that one method is the single place to change so the event automatically carries the memberId instead \u2014 exactly as the spec anticipates.\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest.coreEventCarriesIdAndIdentifier` test and the full suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`), and the emitted line confirms correct output:\n```\nINFO  AUDIT - {\"seq\":1,\"ownerId\":11,\"customerCode\":\"NSW-16E6609E\",\"membershipLevel\":1,\"event\":\"OWNER_CREATED\"}\n```",
